        bodyEn: "Swakopmund, a town of German colonial architecture set between the dunes and the Atlantic, offers an unexpected contrast before the road to Damaraland. There, wildlife perfectly adapted to the aridity — including rare elephants capable of covering dozens of kilometres between two water points — coexists with rock engravings several millennia old, evidence of ancient human presence in one of the planet's most extreme environments.",
